{"decision": {"arguments_json": "{\"analysis\":\"Used all six candidate slots on audited development data from 2021\u20132024. Selected d0c5a4f200ae76c68d816a58e59046d74c324f252e21c4005f6fefae0a298e05: trend 20/100, mean-reversion lookback 20 with entry z=-1.5 and exit z=0, allocator reliability window 63 and volatility window 60. Versus the fixed baseline, median validation Sharpe increased from 0.6672 to 0.7929, median annualized turnover fell from 58.4705 to 50.1776 (14.2%), and worst validation drawdown fell from 36.23% to 34.34%. Performance was uneven: selected fold returns were 29.89%, 45.45%, -0.37%, and -0.62%, versus baseline 11.02%, 11.04%, 15.54%, and 7.93%. Thus the aggregate improvement comes from 2023; the selected strategy underperformed the baseline in both 2024 folds. Replay passed with all fold metrics and execution artifacts byte-identical and zero model calls. Generate visual equity and candidate comparisons alongside these fold-level tradeoffs.\",\"risks\":\"Selection and evaluation used the same development research process, creating selection bias across six tested candidates; the final holdout remains unopened and no future profitability is established. Selected fold annualized volatility ranged from 49.54% to 58.63%, and worst drawdown remained substantial at 34.34%. Lower median turnover did not consistently lower costs: selected annualized cost drag was 16.36%, 8.19%, 6.85%, and 8.65%, versus baseline 12.41%, 4.34%, 11.09%, and 13.35%; selected costs were higher in both 2023 folds. Fold 2 drawdown also increased slightly, from 33.98% to 34.05%. Reproducible execution does not establish predictive validity. The cross-source audit corroborated only 21 historical closes; snapshot hashes establish consistency, not market truth or source independence.\",\"next_actions\":\"Preserve the selected parameters, audited data commitments, and replay artifacts. Review the generated equity and candidate visuals with particular attention to the two losing 2024 folds, drawdowns, and cost sensitivity. Before any deployment decision, use a separately authorized, prespecified out-of-sample assessment and execution-cost stress testing; do not retune on the unopened holdout or infer future profit from development results.\"}", "reason": "The candidate budget is exhausted, selected and baseline tradeoffs are inspected, and replay passed. Generate the required visual evidence-based report before finishing.", "tool": "write_report"}, "event": "decision", "step": 7}
